# LATENT findings of scripts/vpn-bot-host-check that are accepted on purpose.
#
# LATENT = the effective value is right now, but a loser that is neither repo-managed
# nor vendor holds another value: remove the winner and the value silently flips.
# This file is the ONLY sanctioned way to accept one; there is no ALLOW_* knob.
# An entry silences exactly the LATENT row with this path and key — nothing else.
#
# Format, one entry per line ('#' starts a comment line):
#   <path>|<key>|<reason, at least 20 characters>
# path  the file the LATENT row names (the loser, a foreign drop-in, or the file that
#       wins at `sysctl --system`)
# key   the row's key: the sysctl key, the lower-case sshd keyword, Section.Key of a
#       systemd *.conf, or the unit name for a foreign drop-in
# tests/test_host_check.py checks the format, as for known-unmanaged.list.
#
# Empty on purpose: under the vendor rule (docs/host-state.md#effective-state) neither
# host has a LATENT left to accept (sweep of 2026-11-11).
